From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the engine asks Google for nothing at start

An engine started with a fresh profile and left on about:blank asked
Google for 21 components, most for Chrome features the engine has no UI
for, then for the time and for whether AI Mode is offered, and kept a
connection to www.google.com open.

- RegisterComponentsForUpdate registers Widevine, CRLSet, PKI metadata,
  origin trials, the autoplay preload list, hyphenation, Screen AI and
  component extensions only.
- CrxUpdateService::RegisterComponent refuses any other component,
  wherever it is registered.
- kNetworkTimeServiceQuerying is off: the system clock is the time.
- kAimEnabled is off: no /async/folae request asking whether AI Mode is
  offered.
- On-device models (kDomicileOnDeviceModels, off) are never registered,
  so their manifest and the gigabytes after it are never downloaded.
- kPreconnectToSearch is off, and the field trial testing config's
  PreconnectToSearchDesktop study, which turned it back on, is dropped:
  no connection to the search engine before anyone searches.

guard-engine-stays-quiet.sh checks it.
---
